Table~\ref{tab:cv_questionnaire} presents repeated $5 \times 10$ Stratified Cross-Validation results across all cohorts. The simple Benchmark Scoring Rule achieves 100.0\,\% $\pm$ 0.0\,\% across all 50 folds on every cohort. In contrast, complex Machine Learning stacking ensembles achieve 99.10\,\% on Adult, 95.37\,\% on Adolescent, and 97.71\,\% on Child cohorts. Complex statistical learners underperform the integer baseline due to finite-sample boundary estimation error on small cohorts. On these benchmarks, machine learning adds zero incremental predictive value over basic addition.

