Disaggregating performance across scanning centers demonstrates substantial acquisition heterogeneity. Site SDSU achieved 82.4\,\% accuracy ($14/17$ correct), whereas PITT achieved 46.0\,\% ($23/50$) and OHSU achieved 48.0\,\% ($12/25$). Due to small sample size ($N=17$), SDSU's confidence interval spans $[59.0\,\%, 93.8\,\%]$. After controlling the family-wise error rate across the four tested centers via the Holm-Bonferroni step-down procedure, SDSU's adjusted significance is $p_{\text{adj}} = 0.0509 > 0.05$. Consequently, no individual scanning center demonstrates statistically significant above-chance accuracy after multiplicity correction.

